  "skip_reason": "dimensional_split rules (ESS RFC §7.5) are not yet materializable by the ESS discretize pipeline. The rule engine dispatches stencil and replacement forms; the `kind: dimensional_split` composite requires a sweep-loop-level expansion that ESD owns (src/operators/transport_2d.jl::transport_2d_linrood!). Once ESS gains structural support for dimensional_split — consuming the `axes`, `inner_rule`, and `splitting` fields to orchestrate per-axis 1D sweeps — this fixture should verify that the declarative pipeline output matches the imperative reference to machine precision on a smooth 2D initial condition (see manufactured_solution_proposed below).",
  "manufactured_solution_proposed": "q(xi, eta, t) = 1 + 0.5*sin(2*pi*xi/L_xi)*sin(2*pi*eta/L_eta) advected by a steady divergence-free wind field on a c24 cubed-sphere panel. At t=0 with small dt, the tendency from the declarative rule should match transport_2d_linrood!(tendency, q, vel_xi, vel_eta, grid, dt) to machine precision (relative error < 1e-12). See test/test_transport_2d.jl for the imperative reference tests that pin the same invariants.",
  "grids_proposed": [
